Spec: Private owned frpc bridge

Purpose:
  Authenticate the actual owned runtime through a private pipe and carry its approved application scope over Agent-held mTLS.

Owns:
  ./FrpRuntimeBridge.cs

References:
  ./RuntimePipe.sdd
  /control-auth/dotnet/LinkGate.Authority/ControlClient.sdd
  /windows/LinkGate.Processes/LinkGate.Processes.sdd

Must:
  Register the bridge with its session before launch; serialize child assignment with stop so a child cannot escape a concurrent shutdown.
  Reserve the protected pipe before launching and hold the verified child and Job before accepting runtime bytes.
  Check the OS pipe client PID against the held live child before network use and after TLS setup; reject other processes without external delivery.
  Derive application identity and permission generation from the approved local review and require an explicit publish/access role.
  Connect only to the configured IPv4 server, validate normal owner chain/name and fixed server SPKI, and write the fixed scope preface before forwarding frpc bytes.
  Keep private keys in platform handles, bound connections and handshakes, and abort raw sockets before awaiting canceled copies.
  Stop this runtime and all bridge connections when local approval changes, the child exits, identity expires or the owner stops; pending updates/rejections preserve unchanged approval.
  Pass only an explicitly supplied canonical numeric IPv4 STUN endpoint snapshot to the child; never inherit a public discovery list from the parent environment.
